Stop and remove the named shared services' containers, or all of them, found by
their labels from any checkout of the repository: no treerig.toml is needed.
Their data and pinned ports are kept; --volumes deletes the data and releases
the ports, and asks you to confirm, as `worktree remove` does. It does not ask
whether worktrees are using them.

Usage:
  treerig shared down [name...] [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help                     help for down
      --label-namespace string   supply the Docker label namespace when there is
                                 no usable treerig.toml to say it
      --volumes                  also delete the data volumes and release the
                                 pinned ports
      --yes                      skip the confirmation phrase

Global Flags:
      --config string   path to treerig.toml (default: nearest above cwd)
  -V, --version         output the version number
